Insert the new node between the <bold>next</bold> pointer and the node pointed by it. This operation is used by lists to link new nodes to the list head. The new node&apos;s <computeroutput>previous_</computeroutput> pointer is set to the current node, and its <computeroutput>next_</computeroutput> pointer is set to the current node&apos;s <computeroutput>next_</computeroutput>. The neighbouring nodes are updated to point to the new node, maintaining the integrity of the double-linked list. </para>
